spans.s:
(प्र-√ उक्ष्) P. प्रोक्षति to sprinkle upon, besprinkle, consecrate (for sacrifice), RV.; VS.; ŚBr.; GṛŚrS.;
to sacrifice, kill, slaughter (a sacrificial victim), MBh.; R. :
Caus. प्रोक्षयति, to sprinkle, besprinkle, Suśr.

प्रोत्-√ सृ (प्र-उद्-√ सृ) P. -सरति, to pass away, disappear, be gone, Caṇḍ. :
Caus. -सारयति, ˚ते, to drive away, disperse, dispel, destroy, MBh.; Hariv.; Mṛcch.;
to urge on, exhort, incite, MW.;
to grant, offer (see below).

cl. 1. P. Ā. (Dhātup. xxi, 6) प्रोथति, ˚ते, to be equal to or a match for, be able to withstand (gen. or dat.), Bhaṭṭ.;
 (P.) to be full, L.;
to destroy, subdue, overpower, W. (cf. √ प्रुथ्).

प्रोन्-√ मील् (प्र-उद्-√ मील्) P. -मीलति, to open the eyes, Bhaṭṭ.;
to open (as a flower), blossom, Prab.;
to come to light, appear, Cat. :
Caus. -मीलयति, to open (the eyes), Kathās.;
to unfold, reveal, manifest, Cat.

(प्र-√ ऊर्णु) P. Ā. प्रोर्णोति, or ˚णौति;
 ˚णुते, to cover, veil, envelop, AV.; TS.; KātyŚr.; Bhaṭṭ.;
 (Ā.) to be covered or veiled, VS.; TS.; Br.; Kauś. :
Intens. प्रोर्णोनूयते, to cover completely, Bhaṭṭ. (cf. Pāṇ. iii, 1, 23,

प्रोल्-√ लस् (प्र-उद्-√ लस्; only P. pr. p. प्रोल्लसत्),
to shine brightly, glitter, Śiś.;
to sound, be heard, Kathās.;
to move to and fro, Kathās.

(प्र- √ 1. ऊह्) P. प्रोहति, to push forward or away, VS.; KātyŚr.; Nir.;
to throw down, KātyŚr.;
to effect or bring about by transposition, TāṇḍBr.
